+# stream
+
+Python tools for reading NFS Carbon (Black Box) data files, mainly the stream file
+`STREAML5RA.BUN`. One folder for each topic. Folders match `CARBON_STREAM_ROADMAP.md`
+in NFS-ModTools. Each tool runs on its own; there is no launcher.
+
+## Layout
+
+| Folder | Topic | File | Roadmap |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `common/` | Chunk envelope, hashing, chunk inventory, chunk registry and probe, outputs helper | both | Shared base |
+| `scenery/` | Scenery info, instances, override groups, DAE-to-Blender matching | stream | Tier 1, items 1-3 |
+| `solids_materials/` | Solid/mesh reader, material dictionary viewer | stream | Tier 1, item 4 |
+| `flares/` | SolidMarkers (0x13401A) flares and flare packs | stream | Tier 1, item 5 |
+| `texture_anim/` | UV scroll and TextureAnimPack frame-swap | stream | Tier 1, item 7 |
+| `world_anim/` | world_anim chunks 0x37220-0x37270 | stream | Parser closed, playback open |
+| `emitters/` | EmitterLibrary / WorldFXTrigger to BeamNG particles | stream | Tier 2, port closed |
+| `triggers/` | Ambient audio event triggers (0x80036000 family) | stream | Tier 2, set aside |
+| `region/` | Region file parsers: relations, CARP, TrackPath | region | Out of scope |
+| `viewers/` | Region viewer and 3D viewer (use stream and region code) | both | Support |
+| `outputs/` | All generated and downloaded data. Local only, ignored by git | - | - |
+
+## Run
+
+Run each script from the repo root, for example:
+
+    python common/chunk_registry.py STREAML5RA.BUN --kind stream
+    python common/chunk_probe.py STREAML5RA.BUN 0x0003410D
+    python flares/flare_scenery_scan.py --help
+
+Most scanners accept `--help`. Each script has a docstring with the layout it reads.
+`tools.md` has one line for every tool. `tool_gaps.md` lists what each tool does not read.
+
+## Outputs rule
+
+Every tool writes generated files to `outputs/<tool-name>/`. Git ignores `outputs/`.
+Data files such as `hashes_main.txt`, `fx_triggers.tsv`, and dumps also stay in `outputs/`
+(local only). New tools get their folder from `common/nfs_outputs.py`:
+
+    from nfs_outputs import out_path
+    out_path("my_tool", "result.tsv")      # outputs/my_tool/result.tsv
+
+## Imports
+
+Scripts import shared modules by flat name (`from nfs_region_common import ...`).
+Each script that needs a shared module starts with a short bootstrap that adds
+`common/`, `region/`, `scenery/`, and `solids_materials/` to `sys.path`.
+When you add a script that imports one of these modules, copy the bootstrap from any
+existing script. New shared modules go in `common/`.
